---
import PolicyLayout from '../layouts/PolicyLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig, withBase } from '../data/site';

const sections = [
  { id: 'scope', label: 'Scope and responsibility' },
  { id: 'core-bot-data', label: 'Data handled by the core Bot' },
  { id: 'activity-data', label: 'Data handled by AK Guesser' },
  { id: 'discord-access', label: 'Discord permissions and data access' },
  { id: 'use', label: 'How data is used' },
  { id: 'sharing', label: 'Sharing and service providers' },
  { id: 'retention', label: 'Retention and security' },
  { id: 'choices-contact', label: 'Choices, deletion, and contact' },
];
---

<PolicyLayout
  pageTitle="Privacy Policy"
  description="How The Mayling Bot and its AK Guesser Activity handle information."
  lead="This policy separates the core Bot from AK Guesser and explains the information handled by each."
  active="privacy"
  sections={sections}
>
  <section id="scope">
    <h2><span>1</span> Scope and responsibility</h2>
    <p>
      This Privacy Policy explains how <strong>The Mayling Bot</strong> (Discord application ID
      {' '}<code>{siteConfig.appId}</code>) handles information. Capitalized terms have the meanings given in the
      {' '}<a href={withBase('terms/#agreement')}>Terms of Service</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      The Service contains two parts: the private core Bot used in Selected Servers and AK Guesser, an Activity
      contained within the same Discord application. The Operator is responsible for the
      practices described here.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="core-bot-data">
    <h2><span>2</span> Data handled by the core Bot</h2>
    <p>Depending on the features enabled in a Selected Server, the core Bot handles these categories:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Server and channel information:</strong> server IDs, channel IDs, allowed-channel settings, and related Discord context.</li>
      <li><strong>Member and role information:</strong> User or member IDs, usernames or nicknames, role IDs, and stored member-role assignments.</li>
      <li><strong>Message and command information:</strong> message text and related identifiers used to recognize prefix commands and Operator-managed triggers.</li>
      <li><strong>Configuration information:</strong> prefixes, Operator-managed trigger settings, role-feature settings, channel settings, and other enabled configuration.</li>
      <li><strong>Operational information:</strong> command use, audit or error records, and identifiers needed to secure, troubleshoot, and maintain the core Bot.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The core Bot accesses, uses, or retains these categories only when needed for an enabled feature, security, troubleshooting, or service operation.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="activity-data">
    <h2><span>3</span> Data handled by AK Guesser</h2>
    <p>AK Guesser may handle:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Discord identity:</strong> the Player's Discord user ID, username, and avatar.</li>
      <li><strong>Activity context:</strong> relevant Selected Server, channel, and Activity-instance identifiers.</li>
      <li><strong>Game information:</strong> typed guesses, progress, results, scores, timing, streaks, history, and the identifier of a posted result.</li>
      <li><strong>Preferences:</strong> reminder choice and channel, time zone, theme, audio, transitions, and other interface settings.</li>
      <li><strong>Session and operational information:</strong> a hashed session credential, expiry, IP-based rate-limit information, request details, and error records.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      AK Guesser uses Discord sign-in to obtain the Player's Discord user ID, username, and avatar. Temporary Discord
      sign-in tokens are used only to authenticate the Activity and are not stored in the Service database.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="discord-access">
    <h2><span>4</span> Discord permissions and data access</h2>
    <p>
      The core Bot can read messages in Discord channels where it has access so it can recognize prefix commands and
      Operator-managed triggers. It may receive message text and related identifiers needed for those features.
    </p>
    <p>
      The core Bot can also receive member and role information from Selected Servers to operate member-role
      features. Some message-content access and member data require Discord's Message Content or Guild Members
      privileged gateway intents. The Service uses this access only for the features described here and for
      necessary security and troubleshooting.
    </p>
    <p>
      AK Guesser uses Discord sign-in to identify the correct Player and associate that account with game state
      and settings.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="use">
    <h2><span>5</span> How data is used</h2>
    <p><strong>The core Bot</strong> uses information to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>respond to commands, Operator-managed triggers, and configured features;</li>
      <li>maintain server, channel, prefix, and member-role configuration; and</li>
      <li>secure the core Bot, diagnose failures, and maintain reliability.</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>AK Guesser</strong> uses information to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>authenticate the correct Player and maintain game progress, results, statistics, and settings;</li>
      <li>post the automatic completion result in the launch channel;</li>
      <li>send reminder mentions only when the Player enables them; and</li>
      <li>prevent abuse, secure sessions, and diagnose failures.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Both parts may also process information to comply with Discord requirements and valid legal obligations.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="sharing">
    <h2><span>6</span> Sharing and service providers</h2>
    <p>Information may be disclosed only as needed:</p>
    <ul class="provider-list">
      <li><strong>To Discord</strong> — to receive commands and account or server context, validate Activity sessions, and post automatic results or enabled reminders.</li>
      <li><strong>To hosting, database, storage, security, and logging providers</strong> — which process information on the Operator's behalf to run and protect the Service.</li>
      <li><strong>To Closure Wiki</strong> — when AK Guesser requests artwork or reveal metadata. Ordinary web-request information may be processed when content is served, but no Discord account identifier is intentionally included in those requests.</li>
      <li><strong>When legally required</strong> — in response to valid legal process or when reasonably necessary to protect Users and the Service.</li>
      <li><strong>During a Discord-approved ownership transfer</strong> — to the approved successor Operator, which assumes the applicable obligations for the Service and its Discord API data.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Completing an AK Guesser run automatically posts a result summary in the Activity's launch channel, where
      Discord and people with access to that channel can receive it. Reminder mentions are sent only when enabled.
    </p>
    <p>The Service does not sell Discord API data or share it with advertisers or data brokers.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="retention">
    <h2><span>7</span> Retention and security</h2>
    <p>
      Except where applicable law requires retention, Discord API data is promptly deleted when it is no longer
      needed for the Service's stated functionality, when Discord or the relevant User requests deletion, or when
      the Service stops operating.
    </p>
    <ul class="retention-list">
      <li><strong>Core Bot:</strong> server configuration and member-role records are kept while needed in a Selected Server, subject to the deletion rule above.</li>
      <li><strong>Messages:</strong> message content is processed when the core Bot handles a command, trigger, or enabled workflow. Content or identifiers retained for a configured feature, audit record, or troubleshooting are kept only while that purpose remains necessary.</li>
      <li><strong>AK Guesser:</strong> account-linked game history and settings are kept while needed to provide progress and statistics and are deleted after a verified request or when the Activity no longer needs them.</li>
      <li><strong>AK Guesser sessions:</strong> session credentials stop working eight hours after they are issued. The Service stores only a hash of each credential. An expired hash is not accepted for authentication but may remain stored until the retention process removes it.</li>
      <li><strong>Operational logs:</strong> request, error, and security logs have retention separate from the eight-hour session lifetime and are kept only while needed for security or troubleshooting.</li>
      <li><strong>Discord posts:</strong> result and reminder messages follow Discord's and the Selected Server's retention controls after they are posted.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Reasonable safeguards are used to protect stored Discord data, including hashed Activity session credentials
      and server-side validation. These safeguards are designed to reduce the risk of unauthorized access, loss, or misuse.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="choices-contact">
    <h2><span>8</span> Choices, deletion, and contact</h2>
    <p>
      Users may stop using features, disable reminders, or deauthorize AK Guesser. Server Administrators may
      restrict the Service's permissions, disable available features, or remove it from their Selected Server.
      Because the core Bot is private and unlisted, Users and Server Administrators cannot independently reinstall or authorize it elsewhere.
    </p>
    <p>
      A User may request access to, correction of, or deletion of account-linked data. A Server Administrator may
      request deletion of Selected Server configuration. Reasonable verification may be required. For security,
      include only the Discord user ID or server ID needed to locate the relevant records. Do not include passwords,
      bot tokens, OAuth tokens, or other credentials.
    </p>
    <p>Send privacy and deletion requests to <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contactEmail}`}>{siteConfig.contactEmail}</a>.</p>
    <p>
      Revoking AK Guesser's Discord authorization prevents AK Guesser from using that authorization unless the User
      authorizes it again. Revocation does not itself delete existing account-linked game history or prevent the
      core Bot from processing data in a Selected Server. A User may request deletion of data linked to their account.
    </p>
    <p>
      Removing the core Bot from a Selected Server stops it from receiving new bot events from that server. Removal
      does not itself delete retained data. Users may request deletion of data linked to them, and a Server
      Administrator may request deletion of retained server configuration.
    </p>
    <p>
      The Service is not directed to anyone below Discord's applicable minimum age. The Operator does not
      independently collect or verify age. If the Operator learns that the Service obtained Discord API data from
      someone below that age, the Operator will promptly stop processing and delete that data, except where
      applicable law requires otherwise.
    </p>
    <p>
      This policy will be updated when data categories, purposes, recipients, retention, or deletion choices
      materially change. Routine feature changes that remain within these descriptions do not require a rewrite.
    </p>
  </section>
</PolicyLayout>
